      "content": "It is completely understandable that you feel that way when you've put so much effort into trying to fix things without relief. That feeling of performance is incredibly draining, and it speaks to a deep level of burnout. Sometimes, the exhaustion isn't something to be 'fixed' but rather something that needs to be acknowledged and gently rested alongside. Can you allow yourself a tiny moment today just to exist without the pressure to be 'doing' anything?",
      "source": "target",
